infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Two I/O paths, two concurrency limits
  desc Network sockets scale on epoll/kqueue; fs/crypto/dns/zlib share a 4-slot threadpool
  compares
    - label Network I/O (poll phase)
      children
        - label No threadpool — epoll / kqueue
          desc Kernel signals socket readiness; callbacks run in the poll phase
        - label ~10,000+ idle sockets cost nothing
          desc One JS thread scales to tens of thousands of concurrent sockets
        - label Bounded by the kernel, not by 4
          desc Network concurrency never queues behind pool slots
    - label Threadpool I/O (fs / crypto / dns / zlib)
      children
        - label 4 pool slots by default
          desc UV_THREADPOOL_SIZE, read once at startup, max 1024
        - label The 5th concurrent op waits
          desc fs.readFile / scrypt / dns.lookup / zlib share the 4 threads
        - label Latency cliff, not a network fault
          desc A burst of 12 hashes runs 4 at a time ≈ 3 waves
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
